caption: Mastery
engine-rule: mastery

Under the standardized numerical Mastery requirements in Section 5.6, Atavistic Mastery requires HT 20, at least 100 character points invested in traits purchased through the Tradition after modifiers, excluding Talents; attribute purchases count when the Engine or Tradition explicitly grants their purchase as part of its advancement, consequential use of Atavistic traits serving at least three materially different functions, and one Source-defining deed that the practitioner's original Species could not have accomplished without supernatural assistance and that is recognizably attributable to the fixed Source.

A Tradition may additionally require completion of a required body package, Source Profile, template, acquisition milestone, Path benchmark, or other objective embodiment threshold. Such completion is Tradition-defined rather than universal.

Mastery grants only the higher caps, post-Mastery purchases, new acquisition permissions, or other benefits explicitly written by the Tradition and qualifies the practitioner for the normal Super advancement associated with a mastered Tier 2 Tradition. It does not automatically grant a Mythic list, a new Source, a Power Talent, Alternate Form, Morph, Unkillable, Regeneration, unrelated abilities, or free character points.
